==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Jurassic Cat Sitter''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Catasaurus''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Jurassic Cat's [[Critical Hit]] ability makes it ideal against [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] enemies. The chance is immensely low, at a measly 5%, but this is offset by its quick recharge time and attack rate, which allow stacks to build up and tens of hits to come out in quick succession. However, even against Metal enemies, it might not be useful at times: most of the stronger Metal enemies, such as [[Super Metal Hippoe]] and [[Sir Metal Seal]], outrange it in its Normal and Evolved forms. Due to the low range and damage against any other traits, its use should be limited to Metal foes, but it is not a ''complete'' waste of a slot if brought as a precaution in a stage where Metals turn out not to appear, as its health (particularly in [[True Form]]) and spammability make it a passable improvised meatshield.

Since Jurassic Cat tends to get knocked back by Super Metal Hippoe and Sir Metal Seal before it can hit them, don't rely on it as your only [[:Category:Critical Hit Cats|Critical Hitter]] in stages like [[Fish Hell (Insane)|Fish Hell]], [[Dead Falls]] and [[Utopia is Over There]]; support it with longer-ranged Critters that can land attacks on these enemies more consistently, such as [[Space Cat (Rare Cat)|Space Cat]].

It also has easily accessible and universally useful [[Cat Combo]]s that should not be ignored.

==='''True Form'''===
Catasaurus gains improved health, attack power, range and Critical Hit chance. The range, by going from 150 to 180, is actually a big improvement, as it now allows Catasaurus to outrange both Sir Metal Seal and Super Metal Hippoe. The other stat boosts and better Crit chance further increase survivability and the kill power of a stack, making this unit considerably more consistent and capable of standing up to just about any metal enemy if properly supported by the likes of [[Primordial Cat (Rare Cat)|Modern/Future Cat]] or [[Rope Jump Cat (Rare Cat)|Noodle Cats]].

==='''Talents'''===
Critical chance up is by far the most important talent, as it is both a big and cheap improvement to Catasaurus' offensive power and reliability against Metal enemies. Its Cost Down talent also reduces the strain on your wallet, which is very important in Metal-heavy stages in general. Resist Knockback isn't useful as it only hurts Catasaurus's ability to reposition. The stat buffs and the [[Talent Orbs|Talent Orb]] slot can easily combine with a good base level and allow Catasaurus to still form stacks against buffed Metal enemies and quickly kill even the toughest Metal Seals around.

==='''Orb'''===
Defense Up against Metal. Nothing else would make sense. Catasaurus specializes against Metal enemies, and Defense Up is the only type of Talent Orb for Metal. Almost none of the ability orbs are that useful on Catasaurus compared to other units either. Death Mini-Surge has the potential to crit Metal Doges and other low-HP Metal threats, but is very unreliable. Dodge Attack works well for general survivability in mixed stages, but loses out to Defense Up in every other relevant scenario.

