==Trivia==
*Prior to [[Version 4.7 Update|Version 4.7]], Jurassic Cat was a part of two other [[Cat Combo]]s: [[Baby on Board (Removed Combo)|Baby on Board]] and [[Childs Play (Removed Combo)|Childs Play]].
*Prior to [[Version 15.7 Update|Version 15.7]], Jurassic Cat's descriptions read as follows:
<pre>Jurassic Cat
Descendant of an Ancient Cat Race that
existed during the Jurassic Age.
Might perform Critical attacks</pre>
<pre>Jurassic Cat Sitter
Descendant of an Ancient Cat Race that
takes care of the young during the Jurassic Era.
Might perform Critical attacks</pre>
**Catasaurus's description was unchanged.
*In spite of Jurassic Cat's description, there were no cats in the Jurassic Period. The oldest fossil of a remotely cat-like creature is around 30 million years old, while the Jurassic Period ended 145 million years ago.
*The Japanese descriptions of Jurassic Cat Sitter and Catasaurus imply that each of Jurassic Cat's forms is a descendant of the last.
*Jurassic Cat's Spanish name, Ronronícola, is a pun on ''ronron'', the Spanish onomatopoeia for a cat's purr, and ''cavernícola'', the Spanish word for caveman.
*Jurassic Cat is an example of the [https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/RockBeatsLaser Rock Beats Laser] trope, using extremely primitive weaponry to land [[Critical Hit]]s on [[:Category:Metal Enemies|cyborgs]] augmented with far more advanced technology.
*Catasaurus resembles and references [[mariowiki:Yoshi|Yoshi]] from the ''[[mariowiki:Super Mario (series)|Super Mario]]'' games: its description says "Discovered a cute dinosaur in a magical land of fungi", alluding to the Mushroom Kingdom. When jumping, the dinosaur moves its feet for extra time in the air when attacking, just like Yoshi. It is also interesting to note that when knocked back, the dinosaur's tongue can be seen, which further supports its resemblance with Yoshi.
*It is the only unit with a Talent that costs a mere 25 NP to fully upgrade.

